WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:07.168
First, you write a program once as one clear blueprint, and the computer generates matching code across languages.

2
00:00:07.508 --> 00:00:15.097
Second, every possible input must have a declared outcome up front, preventing hidden crashes before anything runs.

3
00:00:15.437 --> 00:00:21.596
Third, every repair that passes the checker is saved and reused, so you never pay twice for one fix.
